Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.75,0:00:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, I'm Shimin. My project asks whether a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.91,0:00:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,sailboat should learn to sail or plan
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.87,0:00:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,every move, and what each choice costs.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.23,0:00:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This is SailGym, my sailing simulator. Its
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.55,0:00:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,physics engine is built with Rust for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.31,0:00:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,high-speed RL training, and this is an
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.31,0:00:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,interactive web frontend. I control only
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.63,0:00:19.99,Default,,0,0,0,,two things: how fast the rudder turns and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.99,0:00:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,how fast the sail comes in. The physics does
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.63,0:00:25.35,Default,,0,0,0,,the rest. See this
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.35,0:00:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,course. The first mark is straight
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.15,0:00:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,upwind, and the boat can't sail into the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.83,0:00:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,wind, within 45 degrees, it stops,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.11,0:00:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,just like that. That's called being in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.03,0:00:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,irons. So I have to zigzag.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.71,0:00:47.03,Default,,0,0,0,,each turn through the wind is a tack, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.03,0:00:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,a tack done badly leaves the boat stopped
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.99,0:00:50.11,Default,,0,0,0,,and drifting backwards.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.90,0:00:59.74,Default,,0,0,0,,The next gate across the wind
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.34,0:01:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,is easy, point and go. So the gate
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.06,0:01:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,one is my RL, upwind RL task.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.24,0:01:09.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And the second RL task, like
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.44,0:01:11.60,Default,,0,0,0,,the reach one, is the easier one like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.12,0:01:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,So the question is, how do learning from
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.92,0:01:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,experience and planning from model trade
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.08,0:01:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,off success, experience and computation
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.88,0:01:22.88,Default,,0,0,0,,on these tasks? Every controller
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.88,0:01:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,sails the same Rust simulator, sends the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.92,0:01:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,same two rates and gets the same reward,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.32,0:01:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,plus 10 for finishing, minus 10 for
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.00,0:01:31.12,Default,,0,0,0,,failing, minus time and plus distance
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.12,0:01:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,shaping. The learner sees 17 numbers of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.08,0:01:36.04,Default,,0,0,0,,the true boat state, and everything is
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.04,0:01:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,tested on 50 held-out conditions plus 20
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.68,0:01:41.56,Default,,0,0,0,,shifted ones. Okay, so I
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.56,0:01:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,implemented these three algorithms. PPO
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.12,0:01:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,learns on-policy. It collects fresh
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.12,0:01:48.60,Default,,0,0,0,,experience, updates, and throws it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.32,0:01:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,SAC learns off-policy. It keeps
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.48,0:01:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,everything in a replay buffer. Then the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.20,0:01:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,cross-entropy method model predictive
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.20,0:01:58.76,Default,,0,0,0,,control, CEM-MPC, doesn't learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.32,0:02:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,At every decision it just forks the real
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.20,0:02:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,simulator, tries 32 plans, and executes
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.00,0:02:06.44,Default,,0,0,0,,the best first step, spending much in
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.44,0:02:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,computation, but not in experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:11.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And these are the pseudo-code for the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.36,0:02:13.32,Default,,0,0,0,,three. Please pause and read it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.12,0:02:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, so on the reach task, the easy one,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.84,0:02:21.04,Default,,0,0,0,,we found that SAC learns pretty good and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.04,0:02:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,finishes about 3/4 of held-out tests.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.36,0:02:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,But PPO is not that good. About 1 seed in 4
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.32,0:02:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,passes in pilot tests. So you can see PPO is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.96,0:02:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,seed-sensitive but not hopeless. The
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.72,0:02:34.52,Default,,0,0,0,,true model MPC planner and the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.52,0:02:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,handwritten RuleSailor finish every
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.56,0:02:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,time. Then the second,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.37,0:02:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,upwind task, is much harder. For MPC, a
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.37,0:02:44.85,Default,,0,0,0,,two-second horizon never tacks. After
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.85,0:02:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,increasing it to 8 seconds, it can
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.93,0:02:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,finish every run, but at 0.2 seconds per
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.45,0:02:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,decision, it's a lot of computation and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.41,0:02:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,can't be done in real time. And
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.93,0:02:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,PPO and SAC from scratch do not
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.69,0:03:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,finish reliably. 50 demonstrations from
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.69,0:03:03.09,Default,,0,0,0,,our handmade RuleSailor does teach SAC
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.09,0:03:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,to tack in four runs out of 10, but it
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.53,0:03:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,reaches the gate only five times in 150
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.09,0:03:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,tests. So in conclusion,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.97,0:03:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,clearly MPC works, which is a known model
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.57,0:03:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,with foresight, but at a compute cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.77,0:03:19.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And SAC performs better than PPO. The
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.25,0:03:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,next step is trying some standard fixes to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.41,0:03:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,stop SAC's value from blowing up in the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.97,0:03:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,harder task and see whether a learned
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.89,0:03:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,terminal value lets the two-second
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.01,0:03:30.61,Default,,0,0,0,,MPC tack in real time. Thanks.
